==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|wkst|wksht||abbreviation}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|work|sheet}}. First use appears c. 1823 in the publications of {{w|Isaac D'Israeli}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|education}} A [[sheet of paper]] or [[computerized]] [[document]] on which [[problem]]s are [[work out|worked out]] or [[solve]]d and the [[answer]]s are [[record]]ed.
#: {{syn|en|ditto|ditto worksheet}}
# A [[sheet of paper]] [[list]]ing work that is [[complete]]d, to be [[complete]]d or [[in progress]].
#: {{hyper|en|sheet}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2024 January 10|author=Howard Johnston|title=The demise of the 'Deltics'|journal=RAIL|issue=1000|page=45|text=The final outshopping was 55002, which had arrived on October 14 [1980] for a two-month repair, with the usual '''worksheet''' taped to its bodyside stating "to be repainted in two-tone green".}}

