===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[teach]] or [[assess]] [[by means of]] worksheets.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1987|author=Charles R. Chew|title=Reflections by Teachers Who Write|page=65|passage=Both reading and writing were viewed as a series of discreet and essentially uninteresting skills to be described, '''worksheeted''', and tested. Students' own intentions or ability as speakers, listeners, readers, or writers were never a consideration.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Sue Cowley|title=Sue Cowley's A-Z of Teaching|page=117|passage=Lesson after lesson of '''worksheeting''' will quickly leave the children bored and disaffected. The class will also suss out pretty quickly that you're being lazy.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Keen J. Babbage|title=Extreme Students: Challenging All Students and Energizing Learning|passage=Students cannot be textbooked and '''worksheeted''' into mastery, proficiency, brilliance, and commitment.}}

